# Dependencies and build output. dist/ is optional — the launcher runs src/
# directly on Node 22.18+ — and the published package ships source, not dist.
node_modules/
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo

# npm packaging. `npm pack` and a failed `npm publish` both leave a tarball
# sitting in the repo root.
*.tgz

# Secrets. nave itself reads none of these, but nothing else should either.
.env
.env.*

# nave's own working state — memory, transcripts, cache, local agents. All of
# it stays on the machine it was written on and is not published.
#
# NAVE.md at the repo root is NOT ignored: it is the standing brief, it is
# documentation, and it is meant to be read.
#
# Note this is a choice about *this* repository, not advice. In your own
# projects, committing .nave/memory/ is how a team shares context with the
# agent — that is what it is for.
.nave/

# Logs
*.log

# Editors
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~

# Claude Code per-machine overrides. Shared settings.json may be committed;
# settings.local.json is personal by definition.
.claude/settings.local.json

# OS artefacts. Thumbs.db in particular appears the moment icons/ is opened
# in Windows Explorer.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
